    {
      "$comment": [
        "Voltage-stress pillar \u2014 VDE-AR-N 4105 operating point.  Sunny midday: PV runs near nameplate while residential load drops to the morning trough, reversing feeder power flow.  ``vm_pu`` drifts toward the upper bound; without the Q-V droop the constraint monitor must shed real-power injection to recover (lost served energy).  With the droop, local Q absorption keeps voltage in deadband and full PV output is preserved.",
        "Two-row ablation in a single experiment: scare-with-droop vs scare-without-droop on identical (grid, seed, scenario) \u2014 direct attribution of the droop's contribution."
      ],
      "name": "voltage_stress",
      "grids": [
        "simbench_lv"
      ],
      "n_seeds": 15,
      "variants": [
        "scare"
      ],
      "ablations": [
        {},
        {
          "enable_qv_droop": false
        }
      ],
      "scenarios": [
        {
          "kind": "pv_peak",
          "max_failures": 1,
          "priority_assignment": "skewed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "$comment": [
        "Line-loading stress pillar \u2014 exercises the line-thermal constraint pipeline.  Loads are scaled up 1.8x and every PowerLine's ampacity is halved, guaranteeing overload after a single branch failure redirects flow.  Three-row ablation in one experiment: full pipeline vs monitor-off vs reconfig-ranking-off \u2014 direct attribution of each new mechanism.",
        "With the full pipeline: branch-mode monitor fires on overload, sends StartBalanceNegotiation to the lower-priority endpoint group, the reconfigurator's 6c ranking avoids the most-loaded restoration path.",
        "Monitor-off baseline shows what the system does when line overload is silent (the legacy behaviour).  Ranking-off baseline tests whether the priority-aware shedding alone is enough without changing reconfiguration choices."
      ],
      "name": "line_stress",
      "grids": [
        "simbench_lv",
        "simbench_lv_reconfig"
      ],
      "n_seeds": 15,
      "variants": [
        "scare"
      ],
      "ablations": [
        {},
        {
          "enable_line_loading_constraint": false
        },
        {
          "enable_reconfig_feasibility_ranking": false
        }
      ],
      "scenarios": [
        {
          "kind": "line_stress",
          "load_scale": 1.8,
          "ampacity_scale": 0.5,
          "max_failures": 2,
          "priority_assignment": "skewed",
          "slack_budget_pct": 0.45
        }
      ]
    },
